# Flashwork IDE program

Flashwork is a **local-first Tauri 2 + React + Rust** desktop workspace for coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Copilot CLI, Gemini, Antigravity, Mimo, Freebuff) with real PTYs.

The current product (orchestrator, Task Board, MCP/Skills panel, Git control, Graphify, Agent Canvas POC) **stays**. OmniRoute/9router **does not stay** (ADR 009). The in-app IDE workbench **does not stay** (P13 / ADR 011). The program keeps per-project harness/RAG, opaque routing over CLIs + vendor APIs, and a beta N8N-like canvas.

## Hard rules (existing, still in force)

- Do not stop or restart `tauri dev` / Vite if already running.
- Do not commit, push, tag, or release unless the owner asks in that message.
- No AI co-author trailers on commits.
- i18n is mandatory: every visible string in `en.ts` **and** `pt-BR.ts`.
- Changelog under `[Unreleased]` in `apps/orchestrator/docs/CHANGELOG.md` for user-facing work.
- CSS Modules + tokens in `theme.css`. Never hardcode colors. No Tailwind. No gradients / generic template UI.
- English for versioned source, comments, JSDoc, changelog, and docs. Locale files are the exception.

## Planning vs implementation

Until the owner explicitly asks to implement a named plan, **only edit markdown / ADR / memory / Cursor rules**. Do not scaffold the IDE, fork VS Code, or add dependencies.

Entry points:

- Memory: `.claude/memory/MEMORY.md` and `.claude/memory/CONTEXT.md`
- ADRs: `.claude/adr/`
- Spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-17-flashwork-ide-program-design.md`
- Plans: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-17-*.md`
- Existing app guide: `apps/orchestrator/AGENTS.md`

## Architecture decisions already recorded

- Do **not** fork [microsoft/vscode](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode). Use it (and [vscode-docs](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-docs)) as UX and SCM reference. Keep Tauri. See ADR 004.
- Each project lives on a user-chosen disk folder with isolated history, harness, and RAG. See ADR 005.
- The developer should not pick models/tokens; routing is opaque over CLIs and first-party APIs. See ADR 006, 009, 010.
- Do **not** add an in-app Monaco/VS Code workbench. Edit in VS Code via `open_in_vscode`. See ADR 011.
- Canvas (N8N-like) is a **beta tab**, not a replacement for the Task Board. See ADR 007.
- Do not add OpenRouter.com or another LLM gateway.

